<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $15.1 mln Nov 27.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $15.1 mln Nov 27.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $15.1 million deficit on Nov 27 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON NOVEMBER 27</p>
<p>Exports: $154.3 million</p>
<p>Imports: $202.1 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $219.2 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $186.5 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $15.1 million</p>
<p>NOVEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $3.118 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $3.440 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $7.253 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $4.385 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $2.546 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511-2485418</p>
</text>
